{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BsfPLiWJTpZAJ9mCT",
	"notes": "A Weirdboy: an Ork psyker, built on the same Thaumatology: Sorcery chassis as every other psyker in this project (Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq), reskinned Ork-flavour and gated by Warp Empowerment exactly as an Astropath or Librarian is, just tuned for raw destructive power over control. A Weirdboy near a WAAAGH! (framework.md's WAAAGH! Gestalt trait, included as part of Ork Physiology below) treats his own Warp Empowerment as one level higher for the purpose of which known powers he may safely reach for — the mechanical reason Weirdboyz cut loose with Da Jump and Fists of Gork mid-battle instead of only in careful isolation, and why an isolated Weirdboy is far less dangerous than one embedded in his mob.\nPerils of the Warp is unchanged from the human-scale rules (Imperium/ Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq): Catastrophic failure (fail the Will roll by 10+, or roll an unmodified 18) is, for a Weirdboy specifically, the setting's own trope of an exploding head — Codex background and Black Library both play a Weirdboy's head literally detonating as a routine occupational hazard, not a narrative rarity. Ork society's usual answer is to keep a Painboy or Mek \"attendant\" nearby with tools (a wrench, a shock-lash, sometimes a special hat) to relieve the pressure before it gets that far — flavour for play, not a separate mechanic.\nPoint math: Ork Physiology 179 + psychic package 93 (10 Unusual Background + 20 Psyker Talent 2 + 60 Warp Empowerment 5 + 8 Witch-sight - 5 Social Stigma) + powers 92 modified (7 'Eadbanger x2 + 7 Fists of Gork x2 + 18 Warpath + 60 Da Jump) + skills 11 = 375 points, inside framework.md's Senior Agents / low Astartes-adjacent range — a rare, powerful, and dangerous Ork specialist, matching how the fiction treats a proper Weirdboy as a small strategic asset (or liability) in his own right. Da Jump alone needs Warp Empowerment's full level-5 cap (60) with no headroom to spare; a \"young,\" less-developed Weirdboy who hasn't grown into Da Jump yet should drop Warp Empowerment to level 2 (cap 30, saving 30 points) and disable Da Jump until later.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "TVr94LxXu05mj38ek",
			"name": "Ork Physiology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Ork Boy: the baseline greenskin warrior, grown fast, fed on violence, and built to get bigger and meaner the longer it survives. This trait is the shared baseline every growth lens (Nob, Warboss) and every Oddboy specialisation (Mek, Painboy, Weirdboy) builds on top of. Primary sources: Codex: Orks background across editions, Nate Crowley's Ghazghkull Thraka: Prophet of the Waaagh! and Mike Brooks' Brutal Kunnin', calibrated against Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader/Deathwatch/Only War Ork material for relative scale.\n\nDesign: 138 (Attribute Modifiers) + 10 (Thick Hide) + 10 (High Pain Threshold) + 6 (Hard to Kill 3) + 5 (Rapid Healing) + 5 (Injury Tolerance, No Brain) + 15 (Resistant to Disease and Toxins) + 0 (Fungal Physiology) - 10 (Bloodlust) - 10 (Impulsiveness) - 5 (Overconfidence) + 10 (Ork Kunnin' 1) + 5 (WAAAGH! Gestalt) = 179 points of physiology alone, before skills — see the Ork Boy template for a full character, and the growth lenses and Oddboy Talents below for Nobs, Warbosses, Meks, Painboyz and Weirdboyz built on top of it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tYnwz6zQUrzjj4-4C",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Boy)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: ST 22, DX 11, IQ 8, HT 13, HP 26, SM 0. Increased ST +12 (B14, 10/level, 120) for ST 22 — \"stooped but heavy; brawnier than a man\": Basic Lift 96 lb, well past an unaugmented human but nowhere near an Astartes' ST 30. Increased DX +1 (B15, 20/level, 20) for DX 11 — \"far clumsier than a Marine,\" barely above a Guardsman's own DX 12 despite the far greater ST. Decreased IQ -2 (B16, 20/level, -40) for IQ 8, the framework's own figure for \"not smart, but not helpless either\" — offset in play by Ork Kunnin' below rather than by raw IQ. Increased HT +3 (B15, 10/level, 30) for HT 13. Extra Hit Points +4 (B16, 2/level, 8) for HP 26 (22 base from ST, +4): an Ork soaks up more damage than its ST alone would suggest, matching how much punishment a Boy shrugs off in the fiction. 120+20-40 +30+8 = 138 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
